## 3. Know which system owns each responsibility

| System or repository | Responsibility | Keep this distinction clear |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Approved application template** | Generates the initial application. | The template root is not the generated app. |
| **Application source repository** | App code, tests, dependency locks, and native configuration. | Its branch and commit identify what is built. |
| **Platform configuration repository** | Enrollment request and review/promotion history. | Its protected merge identifies the authorized provisioning input. |
| **Provisioning engine** | Implements request validation and live apply. | Developer request YAML does not contain the engine implementation. |
| **Workflow catalog** | Approved immutable template versions and compatibility. | Select a currently approved version, not one copied from a historical run. |
| **Vela** | Executes the configured validation and protected orchestration. | A PR preview is separate from live apply. |
| **Bitrise** | Runs mobile workflows and retains configured artifacts/reports. | Build success alone does not establish distribution. |
| **Danger.js** | Checks the configured PR conventions and provides feedback. | Comments do not replace enforced required statuses. |
| **Sauce Labs** | Executes supported tests on the approved device matrix. | App registration, storage upload, and test-job identities have different meanings. |
| **NowSecure** | Produces configured mobile security assessment evidence. | Submission is not completed assessment; assessment is not binary hardening. |
| **App Management** | Internal distribution, including downstream signing where applicable, enablement, and assignment. | Confirm the exact version and audience at the user endpoint. |
| **Google Play / App Store Connect** | Destination processing and governed testing/publication. | Upload is separate from processing, tester availability, and public release. |

The exact internal request schema and custom step contracts belong in their implementation pages. This overview does not invent YAML fields or step outputs.

## 4. Understand ownership and access

| Role | Performs |
| :--- | :--- |
| **Developer / request author** | Prepare source, run local validation, submit the request, and record source identity. |
| **Reviewer** | Review the exact request revision, access groups, template selection, and intended change. |
| **Platform Engineering** | Own protected provisioning, credential bindings, workflow maintenance, and reviewed recovery. |
| **Authorized Vela operator** | Inspect execution through the approved access path, including VPN where required, and provide sanitized evidence. |
| **QA / business tester** | Verify behavior and access for the intended version and audience. |
| **Application/release owner** | Own destination decisions and applicable release authorization. |

Developers **do not manually create Bitrise apps or handle raw production credentials in the web console**. The request contains configuration; protected automation binds signing material and other approved credentials.

Request only the access needed for your role. Store administration and production-signing access are not universal developer prerequisites.

