## 8. Establish release evidence and safe recovery

The supplied seven-milestone ladder defines the evidence to collect:

| Milestone | Evidence focus |
| :--- | :--- |
| `BuildStarted` | Intended source, branch, route, and inputs. |
| `BuildSuccessful` | Successful execution for the identified build configuration. |
| `ArtifactValidated` | Artifact existence, non-zero size, identity, and cryptographic hash. |
| `Uploaded` | Destination receipt or registered artifact/version identity. |
| `Signed` | Applicable build/distribution signing verification. |
| `Enabled` | Required destination version state. |
| `Assigned & UserVisible` | Intended audience assignment and exact-version visibility. |

This is an evidence checklist, not a universal chronological signing sequence. Signing may occur before upload, downstream after ingestion, or at multiple boundaries. Re-signing or transformation can change bytes; record resulting hashes and artifact lineage.

### Preserve state after an uncertain write

Under the supplied **one-write rule**, do not repeat an external mutation after a timeout or ambiguous response. Stop in the reported partial-failure/unknown state, preserve evidence, and use the approved read-only reconciliation procedure before further writes.

Do not delete/recreate the Bitrise app, replay the protected merge, replace signing credentials, or retry a route as an assumed repair. One negative read may be inconclusive when the destination is eventually consistent.

## 9. Apply the workshop lessons throughout this section

The workshop supplies practical guidance for repository generation, request review, Vela inspection, promotion, route verification, and safe recovery. Those instructions appear in their relevant pages; the walkthrough brings the exercise together without duplicating the procedures.

The **28 October 2026 reference canary** showed:

| Route | Historical evidence |
| :--- | :--- |
| QA Android | Distribution signing, enablement, assignment, and exact-version user visibility were confirmed. |
| QA iOS | Bitrise build passed, but downstream App Management signing failed with `distribution_signing_failed`. Publication was not established. |
| UAT Android / iOS | Publication was not confirmed in the apply result. |

The apply outcome was a **partial failure**. The signing problem was accepted as a known issue for that exercise; its underlying cause was not established. Preserve the confirmed Android outcome while reconciling the iOS result.

This historical run does not establish current platform health. Do not reuse its application identity for another create-only enrollment or treat its template version as currently approved.

