# PR, Testing & Security Gates

A gate permits progression only when its required evidence is present and valid for the intended revision, artifact, route, and environment. A comment, report upload, or job submission alone is not a passing gate.

This page connects Danger.js, tests/coverage, Sauce Labs, NowSecure, and release authorization to the [approved pipelines](../bitrise-pipelines/). Test authoring, full feature tests, device configuration, and detailed Sauce Labs troubleshooting belong in **Testing & Quality**.

> **Confidential — internal use only.** Keep credentials and evidence in approved systems. Do not publish raw API responses, private video/artifact URLs, test credentials, sensitive screenshots, or environment dumps. Protected bot and vendor credentials are bound by authorized automation, not copied into PRs or developer source.

## 1. Know the required gates

| Gate | Required evidence | Must not be mistaken for |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **PR health** | Meaningful description, assignee, designated reviewer, and no draft/WIP status when ready to merge. | Two completed peer approvals. |
| **Peer review** | Two peer approvals under the supplied application PR policy, plus applicable ownership rules. | A Danger success comment. |
| **Source checks** | Configured lint, type/static checks, tests, coverage evaluation, and Bitrise build for the current revision. | A report generated from older source. |
| **Device tests** | Required suite completed on the approved matrix against the identified app/test package. | App registration or upload alone. |
| **Security assessment** | Completed assessment and policy decision tied to the assessed binary. | Assessment submission or automatic binary hardening. |
| **Release authorization** | Required TGRC approval before UAT/Production under the supplied company policy. | Automatic authorization from a passing build. |

The supplied security policy blocks **Critical or High** findings. Evaluate the actual severity policy and assessment completeness; findings are not limited to CVEs.

