This reflects the supplied internal distribution journey. Confirm actual operation ordering and prerequisites against the integration contract. Do not assume its signing sequence is the same as a store's processing sequence.

### Readback and user verification

| Check | Required observation |
| :--- | :--- |
| **Ingestion** | Destination accepted the intended artifact and identifies its app/version. |
| **Signing** | Required downstream signature result is confirmed, not inferred from Bitrise. |
| **Enablement** | Intended version has the required active/available state. |
| **Assignment** | Correct approved group or audience is assigned. |
| **Visibility** | An intended user's authorized endpoint/catalog shows the exact version. |
| **Installation/launch, if required** | Verified separately on the approved device, with actual installed version recorded. |

Do not default every app to **All Users**. The source distinguishes general employee apps and business-specific entitlement. Use the approved audience; business-owner approval and entitlement requirements belong to the dedicated distribution guide.

The App Management API, upload/sign/enable/assign step contracts, and authenticated user-endpoint schema were not supplied. No internal endpoint, request payload, or success parser is invented here. Obtain those contracts before implementing the corresponding automation.

